@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+---
+"@x402/extensions": patch
+---
+
+`validateDiscoveryExtension` now validates Bazaar extension info with an interpreting JSON Schema validator (`@cfworker/json-schema`) instead of compiling the route author's schema with Ajv on every call. Ajv's `compile` uses `new Function()`, which Cloudflare Workers forbid during request handling, so on workerd every valid extension was reported as `valid: false` ("Code generation from strings disallowed for this context") and each request paid for a failed compile. The validator now runs identically on Node, bundlers and Workers, never generates code at runtime, and has no per-call compilation step. Well-known string formats (`uri`, `date-time`, …) are now enforced, and a non-object `schema` is rejected explicitly instead of being treated as unconstrained.
